{"version":"6.9","hitCount":1,"request":{"queryString":"TITLE:\"The circadian gene Period2 plays an important role in tumor suppression and DNA damage response in vivo\"","resultType":"core","cursorMark":"*","pageSize":5,"sort":"","synonym":false},"resultList":{"result":[{"id":"12372299","source":"MED","pmid":"12372299","doi":"10.1016/s0092-8674(02)00961-3","title":"The circadian gene Period2 plays an important role in tumor suppression and DNA damage response in vivo.","authorString":"Fu L, Pelicano H, Liu J, Huang P, Lee C.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Fu L","lastName":"Fu","firstName":"Loning","initials":"L","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Molecular and Human Genetics, Baylor College of Medicine, One Baylor Plaza, Houston, TX 77030, USA."}]}},{"fullName":"Pelicano H","lastName":"Pelicano","firstName":"Helene","initials":"H"},{"fullName":"Liu J","lastName":"Liu","firstName":"Jinsong","initials":"J"},{"fullName":"Huang P","lastName":"Huang","firstName":"Peng","initials":"P","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-2152-9152"}},{"fullName":"Lee C","lastName":"Lee","firstName":"Cheng","initials":"C"}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0002-2152-9152"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["recommended_reviews","related_data","wikipedia"]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"1","volume":"111","journalIssueId":1123416,"dateOfPublication":"2002 Oct","monthOfPublication":10,"yearOfPublication":2002,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"Cell","title":"Cell","essn":"1097-4172","issn":"0092-8674","nlmid":"0413066","isoabbreviation":"Cell"},"printPublicationDate":"2002-10-01"},"pubYear":"2002","pageInfo":"41-50","abstractText":"The Period2 gene plays a key role in controlling circadian rhythm in mice. We report here that mice deficient in the mPer2 gene are cancer prone. After gamma radiation, these mice show a marked increase in tumor development and reduced apoptosis in thymocytes. The core circadian genes are induced by gamma radiation in wild-type mice but not in mPer2 mutant mice. Temporal expression of genes involved in cell cycle regulation and tumor suppression, such as Cyclin D1, Cyclin A, Mdm-2, and Gadd45alpha, is deregulated in mPer2 mutant mice. In particular, the transcription of c-myc is controlled directly by circadian regulators and is deregulated in the mPer2 mutant. Our studies suggest that the mPer2 gene functions in tumor suppression by regulating DNA damage-responsive pathways.","affiliation":"Department of Molecular and Human Genetics, Baylor College of Medicine, One Baylor Plaza, Houston, TX 77030, USA.","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["Research Support, U.S. Gov't, P.H.S.","Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't","Journal Article"]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Thymus Gland","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"CY","qualifierName":"cytology"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Animals"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Mice, Inbred C57BL"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Mice"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Neoplasms, Experimental","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","abbreviation":"GE","qualifierName":"genetics"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"DNA Damage"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Genetic Predisposition to Disease"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Cyclin A","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"GE","qualifierName":"genetics"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Cyclin D1","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"GE","qualifierName":"genetics"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Cell Cycle Proteins"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Proto-Oncogene Proteins c-myc","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviati